// A trailing `...` on the type was Ziman's own spelling for a variadic parameter until 2026-10-12,
// when it became the `variadic` keyword (docs/DESIGN.md, two entries). Every benchmark attempt on
// 2026-10-12 that declared one wrote the suffix, and one round-1 attempt wrote Go's prefix form
// instead, so both are still recognised here -- only to be answered with the keyword spelled out,
// rather than with `expected ')', found '..'` several characters from the real question. The same
// reason `f(args...)` is recognised in a call (diag_spread_in_call).
fn total(ns: int...) -> int {
    return 0
}

fn also_total(ns: ...int) -> int {
    return 0
}

fn main() {
    print(total(1, 2))
}
